---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Tileshire" description="Tileshire – a card-based roguelike by Anton Bargman">
  <style>
    h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: normal; color: #f0f0f0; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .subtitle { color: #888; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #555; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; color: #e0e0e0; margin: 1.4rem 0 0.4rem; }
    p { color: #ccc; font-size: 0.97rem; max-width: 560px; }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      background: #1e1e1e;
      border: 1px solid #333;
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      color: #888;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .links { margin-top: 2.5rem; display: flex; gap: 1.2rem; align-items: center; }
    .links a { font-size: 0.88rem; color: #888; display: flex; }
    .links a:hover { color: #c8a96e; }
    .links svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; }
    .widget-wrapper { max-width: 552px; overflow: hidden; }
    .widget-wrapper iframe { max-width: 100%; }
  </style>

  <h1>Tileshire</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A card-based roguelike</p>
  <span class="badge">Early development</span>

  <section>
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>Small tiles. Big scores.</p>
    <p>
      Draw a tile. Study the board. Find the placement that turns three separate roads
      into one big, connected cluster.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tileshire is a tile-placement roguelike deckbuilder. Each run, you draw tiles from
      your deck and lay them down to connect roads, rivers, forests, and towns, chasing
      bigger and bigger scoring clusters. Between levels, earn gold, shop for relics, and
      reshape your deck around whatever strategy is working.
    </p>
    <h3>Five decks, five strategies</h3>
    <p>
      Start gentle with a road-and-forest deck built for learning the rules, then branch
      into a draw-heavy economy deck, a water-clustering scorer, a forest-spawning engine,
      or a town deck that snowballs out of control.
    </p>
    <h3>Deckbuilding meets area control</h3>
    <p>
      Rare and legendary tiles let you draw more cards, spawn new land, reshuffle your
      hand, upgrade tiles already on the board, or duplicate your best scorer. Stack the
      right combination and watch a single connection turn into a huge score.
    </p>
    <h3>Runs that never repeat</h3>
    <p>
      Random draws, shop choices, and relic combinations mean no two shires grow the
      same way twice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      The game is currently in early development. More details coming soon.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Platform</h2>
    <p>Mobile (iOS &amp; Android). More platforms may follow.</p>
  </section>

